IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei1-payment`

-- Tests of ei1-payment.l4 (Act ss 12, 13 and 13.1). Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the
-- section named beside the assertion; none is copied from the module's output. Dates were worked out with a
-- calendar program that is not the encoding. One #ASSERT per line.

§ `s 12(1) benefits may be paid for a week (src:332)`
-- args: a benefit period has been established, the week is a week of unemployment, the week falls in the benefit period
#ASSERT `s 12(1) benefits may be paid to the claimant for the week` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 12(1) benefits may be paid to the claimant for the week` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 12(1) benefits may be paid to the claimant for the week` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 12(1) benefits may be paid to the claimant for the week` TRUE TRUE FALSE)

§ `s 12(2) the general maximum (src:334)`
#ASSERT `s 12(2) the general maximum number of weeks for a reason other than those mentioned in subsection (3)` 26 EQUALS 26
#ASSERT `s 12(2) the general maximum number of weeks for a reason other than those mentioned in subsection (3)` 45 EQUALS 45

§ `s 12(2.1) and (2.2) 50 weeks for benefit periods beginning from 27 September 2020 to 25 September 2021 (src:336-338)`
#ASSERT (`s 12(2.1) the period within which a benefit period must begin for the maximum to be 50 weeks`)'s `first day of the period` EQUALS YMD 2020 9 27
#ASSERT (`s 12(2.1) the period within which a benefit period must begin for the maximum to be 50 weeks`)'s `last day of the period` EQUALS YMD 2021 9 25
#ASSERT `s 12(2.1) the maximum number of weeks for a benefit period that begins during that period` EQUALS 50
-- args: the day the benefit period begins, a claimant under the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations
#ASSERT `s 12(2.1) the maximum number of weeks is 50 for a benefit period that begins during the period` (YMD 2020 9 27) FALSE
#ASSERT `s 12(2.1) the maximum number of weeks is 50 for a benefit period that begins during the period` (YMD 2021 3 14) FALSE
#ASSERT `s 12(2.1) the maximum number of weeks is 50 for a benefit period that begins during the period` (YMD 2021 9 25) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 12(2.1) the maximum number of weeks is 50 for a benefit period that begins during the period` (YMD 2020 9 26) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 12(2.1) the maximum number of weeks is 50 for a benefit period that begins during the period` (YMD 2021 9 26) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 12(2.1) the maximum number of weeks is 50 for a benefit period that begins during the period` (YMD 2021 3 14) TRUE)

§ `s 12(2.3)(a)(i) the period for seasonal workers (src:342)`
#ASSERT (`s 12(2.3)(a)(i) the period within which a benefit period must be established`)'s `first day of the period` EQUALS YMD 2021 9 26
#ASSERT (`s 12(2.3)(a)(i) the period within which a benefit period must be established`)'s `last day of the period` EQUALS YMD 2028 10 7

§ `s 12(2.4) an earlier benefit period considered established within the 260 weeks (src:348)`
-- The current benefit period begins on Sunday 2026-10-25; the 260 weeks before it run from 2021-10-31 to 2026-10-24.
-- args: the earlier benefit period (first day, regular benefits paid or payable, notification received), the first day of the current benefit period
#ASSERT `s 12(2.4) the earlier benefit period is considered to have been established within the 260 weeks` (`ei1 Earlier benefit period` OF (YMD 2021 10 31), TRUE, FALSE) (YMD 2026 10 25)
#ASSERT `s 12(2.4) the earlier benefit period is considered to have been established within the 260 weeks` (`ei1 Earlier benefit period` OF (YMD 2026 10 24), TRUE, FALSE) (YMD 2026 10 25)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 12(2.4) the earlier benefit period is considered to have been established within the 260 weeks` (`ei1 Earlier benefit period` OF (YMD 2021 10 30), TRUE, FALSE) (YMD 2026 10 25))
#ASSERT `s 12(2.4) the earlier benefit period is considered to have been established within the 260 weeks` (`ei1 Earlier benefit period` OF (YMD 2021 10 30), TRUE, TRUE) (YMD 2026 10 25)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 12(2.4) the earlier benefit period is considered to have been established within the 260 weeks` (`ei1 Earlier benefit period` OF (YMD 2026 10 25), TRUE, TRUE) (YMD 2026 10 25))

§ `s 12(2.5) around the same time of year (src:350-355)`
-- The windows for a current benefit period that begins on Sunday 2026-10-25 (each from the first day of the week eight
-- weeks before to the last day of the week eight weeks after the week 52, 104, 156, 208, 260 weeks before):
-- 1: 2025-08-31 to 2025-12-27; 2: 2024-09-01 to 2024-12-28; 3: 2023-09-03 to 2023-12-30; 4: 2022-09-04 to 2022-12-31; 5: 2021-09-05 to 2022-01-01.
#ASSERT `s 12(2.5) the earlier benefit period began during the period around the week that is n times 52 weeks before` (YMD 2025 8 31) (YMD 2026 10 25) 1
#ASSERT `s 12(2.5) the earlier benefit period began during the period around the week that is n times 52 weeks before` (YMD 2025 12 27) (YMD 2026 10 25) 1
#ASSERT NOT (`s 12(2.5) the earlier benefit period began during the period around the week that is n times 52 weeks before` (YMD 2025 8 30) (YMD 2026 10 25) 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 12(2.5) the earlier benefit period began during the period around the week that is n times 52 weeks before` (YMD 2025 12 28) (YMD 2026 10 25) 1)
#ASSERT `s 12(2.5) the earlier benefit period began during the period around the week that is n times 52 weeks before` (YMD 2021 9 5) (YMD 2026 10 25) 5
#ASSERT `s 12(2.5) the earlier benefit period began during the period around the week that is n times 52 weeks before` (YMD 2022 1 1) (YMD 2026 10 25) 5
#ASSERT NOT (`s 12(2.5) the earlier benefit period began during the period around the week that is n times 52 weeks before` (YMD 2022 1 2) (YMD 2026 10 25) 5)
#ASSERT `s 12(2.5) the earlier benefit period is considered to have begun around the same time of year` (YMD 2025 11 2) (YMD 2026 10 25)
#ASSERT `s 12(2.5) the earlier benefit period is considered to have begun around the same time of year` (YMD 2024 11 3) (YMD 2026 10 25)
#ASSERT `s 12(2.5) the earlier benefit period is considered to have begun around the same time of year` (YMD 2023 12 30) (YMD 2026 10 25)
#ASSERT `s 12(2.5) the earlier benefit period is considered to have begun around the same time of year` (YMD 2022 12 31) (YMD 2026 10 25)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 12(2.5) the earlier benefit period is considered to have begun around the same time of year` (YMD 2024 6 2) (YMD 2026 10 25))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 12(2.5) the earlier benefit period is considered to have begun around the same time of year` (YMD 2022 1 2) (YMD 2026 10 25))

§ `s 12(2.3) the seasonal-worker table (src:340-346)`
-- The benefit period begins Sunday 2026-10-25 and is established on 2026-10-27, in a Schedule VI region, with earlier benefit periods.
`ei1 test earlier near 1` MEANS `ei1 Earlier benefit period` OF (YMD 2025 11 2), TRUE, FALSE
`ei1 test earlier near 2` MEANS `ei1 Earlier benefit period` OF (YMD 2024 11 3), TRUE, FALSE
`ei1 test earlier far` MEANS `ei1 Earlier benefit period` OF (YMD 2023 3 5), TRUE, FALSE
`ei1 test earlier near 2 without regular benefits` MEANS `ei1 Earlier benefit period` OF (YMD 2024 11 3), FALSE, FALSE
`ei1 test earlier before the window, no notification` MEANS `ei1 Earlier benefit period` OF (YMD 2021 10 30), TRUE, FALSE
`ei1 test earlier before the window, notified` MEANS `ei1 Earlier benefit period` OF (YMD 2021 10 30), TRUE, TRUE
-- args: the day the benefit period is established, the first day of the benefit period, resident in a Schedule VI region, the earlier benefit periods, the 77.992 criteria were met
-- three earlier periods in the 260 weeks, two of them around the same time of year: yes
#ASSERT `s 12(2.3) the maximum number of weeks is read from the table in Schedule V` (YMD 2026 10 27) (YMD 2026 10 25) TRUE (LIST `ei1 test earlier near 1`, `ei1 test earlier near 2`, `ei1 test earlier far`) FALSE
-- only two earlier periods: no
#ASSERT NOT (`s 12(2.3) the maximum number of weeks is read from the table in Schedule V` (YMD 2026 10 27) (YMD 2026 10 25) TRUE (LIST `ei1 test earlier near 1`, `ei1 test earlier near 2`) FALSE)
-- three earlier periods but only one around the same time of year: no
#ASSERT NOT (`s 12(2.3) the maximum number of weeks is read from the table in Schedule V` (YMD 2026 10 27) (YMD 2026 10 25) TRUE (LIST `ei1 test earlier near 1`, `ei1 test earlier far`, `ei1 test earlier far`) FALSE)
-- three earlier periods but one had no regular benefits paid or payable: no
#ASSERT NOT (`s 12(2.3) the maximum number of weeks is read from the table in Schedule V` (YMD 2026 10 27) (YMD 2026 10 25) TRUE (LIST `ei1 test earlier near 1`, `ei1 test earlier near 2 without regular benefits`, `ei1 test earlier far`) FALSE)
-- paragraph (b) instead: no earlier periods at all, criteria of reg 77.992 met
#ASSERT `s 12(2.3) the maximum number of weeks is read from the table in Schedule V` (YMD 2026 10 27) (YMD 2026 10 25) TRUE EMPTY TRUE
-- not resident in a Schedule VI region: no, even under paragraph (b)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 12(2.3) the maximum number of weeks is read from the table in Schedule V` (YMD 2026 10 27) (YMD 2026 10 25) FALSE EMPTY TRUE)
-- established after 7 October 2028 or before 26 September 2021: no
#ASSERT NOT (`s 12(2.3) the maximum number of weeks is read from the table in Schedule V` (YMD 2028 10 8) (YMD 2028 10 8) TRUE EMPTY TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 12(2.3) the maximum number of weeks is read from the table in Schedule V` (YMD 2028 10 7) (YMD 2028 10 1) TRUE EMPTY TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 12(2.3) the maximum number of weeks is read from the table in Schedule V` (YMD 2021 9 25) (YMD 2021 9 19) TRUE EMPTY TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 12(2.3) the maximum number of weeks is read from the table in Schedule V` (YMD 2021 9 26) (YMD 2021 9 26) TRUE EMPTY TRUE
-- (2.4): an earlier period before the 260 weeks counts only if the claimant was notified of payment or non-payment for a week within them
#ASSERT `s 12(2.3) the maximum number of weeks is read from the table in Schedule V` (YMD 2026 10 27) (YMD 2026 10 25) TRUE (LIST `ei1 test earlier before the window, notified`, `ei1 test earlier near 2`, `ei1 test earlier far`) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 12(2.3) the maximum number of weeks is read from the table in Schedule V` (YMD 2026 10 27) (YMD 2026 10 25) TRUE (LIST `ei1 test earlier before the window, no notification`, `ei1 test earlier near 2`, `ei1 test earlier far`) FALSE)

§ `s 12(2), (2.1) and (2.3) the general maximum (src:334, 336, 340)`
-- args: Schedule I figure, Schedule V figure, the 50-week rule applies, the Schedule V table applies
#ASSERT `s 12(2), s 12(2.1) and s 12(2.3) the maximum number of weeks for a reason other than those mentioned in subsection (3)` 38 45 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 38
#ASSERT `s 12(2), s 12(2.1) and s 12(2.3) the maximum number of weeks for a reason other than those mentioned in subsection (3)` 38 45 TRUE FALSE EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `s 12(2), s 12(2.1) and s 12(2.3) the maximum number of weeks for a reason other than those mentioned in subsection (3)` 38 45 FALSE TRUE EQUALS 45
#ASSERT `s 12(2), s 12(2.1) and s 12(2.3) the maximum number of weeks for a reason other than those mentioned in subsection (3)` 38 45 TRUE TRUE EQUALS 45

§ `s 12(3) the maximum for each reason (src:358-366)`
-- args: the reason, the election under section 23
#ASSERT `s 12(3) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period for the reason` `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)` `the 35-week maximum` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 12(3) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period for the reason` `pregnancy` `the 35-week maximum` EQUALS JUST 15
#ASSERT `s 12(3) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period for the reason` `pregnancy` `the 61-week maximum` EQUALS JUST 15
#ASSERT `s 12(3) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period for the reason` `caring for a new-born or adopted child` `the 35-week maximum` EQUALS JUST 35
#ASSERT `s 12(3) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period for the reason` `caring for a new-born or adopted child` `the 61-week maximum` EQUALS JUST 61
#ASSERT `s 12(3) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period for the reason` `a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine` `the 35-week maximum` EQUALS JUST 26
#ASSERT `s 12(3) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period for the reason` `care or support of a family member` `the 61-week maximum` EQUALS JUST 26
#ASSERT `s 12(3) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period for the reason` `care or support of a critically ill child` `the 35-week maximum` EQUALS JUST 35
#ASSERT `s 12(3) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period for the reason` `care or support of a critically ill adult` `the 61-week maximum` EQUALS JUST 15

§ `s 12(4) maxima for a single pregnancy or placement (src:369-372)`
#ASSERT `s 12(4)(a) the maximum number of weeks for a single pregnancy` EQUALS 15
-- args: the election, the weeks are divided in accordance with section 23
#ASSERT `s 12(4)(b) the maximum number of weeks for the care of one or more new-born or adopted children as a result of a single pregnancy or placement` `the 35-week maximum` FALSE EQUALS 35
#ASSERT `s 12(4)(b) the maximum number of weeks for the care of one or more new-born or adopted children as a result of a single pregnancy or placement` `the 35-week maximum` TRUE EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `s 12(4)(b) the maximum number of weeks for the care of one or more new-born or adopted children as a result of a single pregnancy or placement` `the 61-week maximum` FALSE EQUALS 61
#ASSERT `s 12(4)(b) the maximum number of weeks for the care of one or more new-born or adopted children as a result of a single pregnancy or placement` `the 61-week maximum` TRUE EQUALS 69

§ `s 12(4.01) claims under this Part and under section 152.05 (src:374-376)`
-- args: claims under both, the election, divided
#ASSERT `s 12(4.01) the maximum number of weeks of benefits payable under the Act in respect of the child or children` FALSE `the 35-week maximum` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 12(4.01) the maximum number of weeks of benefits payable under the Act in respect of the child or children` TRUE `the 35-week maximum` FALSE EQUALS JUST 35
#ASSERT `s 12(4.01) the maximum number of weeks of benefits payable under the Act in respect of the child or children` TRUE `the 35-week maximum` TRUE EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `s 12(4.01) the maximum number of weeks of benefits payable under the Act in respect of the child or children` TRUE `the 61-week maximum` FALSE EQUALS JUST 61
#ASSERT `s 12(4.01) the maximum number of weeks of benefits payable under the Act in respect of the child or children` TRUE `the 61-week maximum` TRUE EQUALS JUST 69

